  "summary": "Dependency-confusion beacon posts host metadata to hardcoded bare-IP endpoint",
  "details": "The package is a stub whose main module exports a no-op Proxy and ships no real component. Its only functional code is beacon.cjs, which collects host identifiers (hostname, install path, cwd, node version) and POSTs them to the hardcoded bare-IP endpoint http://185.158.107.175:8787/_ah/dc. The beacon fires at install time via a postinstall script (node beacon.cjs) and again on require() of index.js (require('./beacon.cjs').fire()). The destination is a plain-HTTP bare-IP unassociated with any publisher. The version 99.0.1 and the stub nature are consistent with dependency-confusion namespace squatting against an internal @ppa-web-components scope.",
